    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Project: Service Monitor - Workflow Documentation\n\nOverview:\nThis workflow automatically monitors the health of various company programs (HTTP APIs and SSH services). It runs every hour from 9 AM to 6 PM. If a program fails, it performs a secondary check after 60 seconds to avoid false alarms before sending a notification to the Administration and IT departments.\n\nWorkflow Logic (Step-by-Step):\n\n   1.  DailyCheck (Schedule Trigger): Runs the flow every hour (Cron: 0 0 9-18 * * *).\n\n   2. ListProgram (Code): Creates a dynamic list of programs to monitor. Currently using mock data.\n\n   3. ProgramLoop (Loop Over Items): Processes the list one program at a time to prevent system overload.\n\n   4. RouteHTTP/SSH (Switch): Checks the type field of the current program and routes it to the correct verification branch.\n\n   5 . HTTP Branch:\n - CheckHTTP: Sends a real GET request to the target URL.\n\n- IsHTTPWorking?: Checks if the status code is 200.\n\n - Retry Logic: If it fails, Wait60Sec pauses for 60s, then CheckHTTPRetry tries again. If it fails again, SendAlertHTTP triggers.\n\n   6.  SSH Branch:\n - CheckSSH(Mock): Simulates an SSH command execution.\n\n - IsSSHWorking?: Checks if the status is \"success\".\n\n - Retry Logic: Same as HTTP (Wait60Sec1 ➜ CheckSSH(RetryMock) ➜ SendAlertSSH).\n\n    7. Loop Closure: All final nodes (AllOk, SendAlert...) route back to ProgramLoop so the cycle can process the next program in the list.",
        "height": 528,
        "width": 928
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1152,
        -96
      ],
      "id": "2cddf66e-4005-44e5-a422-e316f19e0055",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Transition to Production (How to replace mock nodes):\n\n1. Replacing SSH Mock:\n- Delete both CheckSSH(Mock) and CheckSSH(RetryMock) nodes.\n\n- Replace them with the native n8n SSH node.\n\n- Configuration: Set the operation to Execute Command. Input the real command (e.g., systemctl is-active [service_name]).\n\n- Credentials: Create an SSH credential with the real server IP, port, and authentication (password or private key).\n\n2. Replacing HTTP Mock URLs:\n\n- Open the ListProgram node and replace the fake URLs (httpbin.org, google.com) with the real corporate API endpoints.\n\n3. Replacing SMTP Credentials:\n\n- In SendAlertHTTP and SendAlertSSH, replace the mock SMTP credentials with the company's real email server credentials.\n\n- Update the \"To Email\" field with the real Administration and IT department addresses.",
        "height": 336,
        "width": 832,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1056,
        464
      ],
      "id": "82153ed1-64d1-4ca2-88de-8684b73d7665",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
